Z||000000||mshill||09-17-1999||11:33 PM||||I purchased a set of poly dogbone bushings and after I removed the ones from my stock dogbone, I realized that the poly ones won't fit.  <P>I purchased the Prothane 7-501-BL "Fiero Torque Strut Bushing Kit 84-88"  from Suspension Restoration (www.suspension.com).<P>My stock strut is cast and has a large ridge in the middle of each hole and the diameter of bushings is about 1/8 inch too small even if the middles were tapered.<P>What the Fiero Store catalog lists for both the V6 an L4 look identical to the ones I got but not the ones I need.<P>Do I need to just bite the bullet and get the <BR>Ulitmate Dogbone or does someone really have poly bushings that fit the OEM V6 dogbone?<BR>||||reg||8
Z||000001||Dave85||09-17-1999||11:40 PM||||I just bought the bushings from the Fiero Store a couple of weeks ago and they fit perfect! Took about 15 min. to install.||||reg||1
Z||000002||SCCA FIERO||09-18-1999||12:44 AM||||There are 2 different dogbones from the factory. One has a continues "rib" around it the other has smooth circular parts, where the bushings go, and a rib in the center section. The dogbone with the rib around the whole thing will accept the bushings and the other will not because it has the taper inside. I think the dogbone that will accept the bushings were put in 88 or 87 and 88 V6 Fieros (not sure about the 4 cylinder cars)....which year/model Fiero do you have?||||reg||3
Z||000003||TOM||09-18-1999||01:49 AM||||I replaced my bushings with the same kit. I was told that the dogbone with the tapered inside was a later model. If you need a dogbone for the bushings you have. $10 plus $4 shipping.||||reg||1
Z||000004||mshill||09-18-1999||03:00 AM||||Sometimes I really despise the car parts aftermarket. It seems that one of every three parts I buy to put on this thing don't fit.<P>Previously, I bought a radiator fan coolant switch.  The $10 Niehoff part wouldn't fit cause it didn't have tapered pipe threads.  Had to go to the Pontiac Dealer and got hosed for $20.<P>Now this dogbone thing.  I got to all the trouble and stink to burn those bushings out and fint out that I am hosed.  Should have just bought the Ultimate to begin with.<P>Tom, I'll take you up on that dogbone offer. See my email...<P>Thanks guys.||||reg||10
Z||000005||PaUL||09-18-1999||07:06 PM||||hey MSHILL, if you are not sending those bushings back, Ill be glad to buy them from you. My dogbone doesnt have the rib, send me email if you want to sell them.||||reg||1
Z||000006||mshill||09-19-1999||12:56 AM||||Paul,<P>I am actaully getting the proper dogbone from Tom above.  I figured I would need to get one anyway since I cannot get replacements for the ones I removed from my stock one.<BR>||||reg||1
